From 618ae254a401531cb8db88b63ad28bc29d8a91b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scada <scada@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:53:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/80] arm64: configs: joan_defconfig: enable SELinux in the
 LSM list

CONFIG_LSM came from the postmarketOS config and left SELinux out, so it
was built but never initialised and Android's init failed to load its
policy and rebooted to the bootloader.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0144VMKxYe33NKa3LLPZNivr
---
 arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
index a94b9eaf4e54..d9f2fc4d58aa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/joan_defconfig
@@ -1332,7 +1332,7 @@ CONFIG_SECURITY=y
 CONFIG_SECURITY_NETWORK=y
 CONFIG_SECURITY_PATH=y
 CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX=y
-CONFIG_LSM="landlock,lockdown,yama,loadpin,safesetid,ipe,bpf"
+CONFIG_LSM="landlock,lockdown,yama,loadpin,safesetid,selinux,bpf"
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_BENCHMARK=m
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DH=m
